   214	which is the behavior `protocol/core.md` sections 9.3 and 10 already require.
   215	
   216	## Security impact
   217	
   218	The profile adds the hardened supervisor, the enforcement-backend adapters, the
   219	capability probes, the domain session channel, and the operating-system or
   220	hypervisor primitives to the trusted computing base, and it requires an
   221	implementation to name every one of them — including a mutable interpreter or
   222	installed package tree it depends on — in a `hardened-tcb-v1` record.
   223	
   224	It does not claim that adversarial Go source is safe, that the Go toolchain is
   225	free of defects, that the compiled artifact is authenticated, that a
   226	same-principal or administrator adversary is excluded, or that side channels are
   227	closed. The compile-only rejection policy of `SECURITY.md` remains mandatory and
   228	is not relaxed by containment.
   229	
   230	Its main security value before any implementation exists is negative: it makes
   231	it impossible to claim a hardened guarantee without an exhaustive probe, an
   232	in-domain self-test, a named backend, a named trusted computing base, a distinct
   233	receipt, marker, and claim version, and a distinct cache identity.
