   541	
   542	### 6.4 The closed hardened capability-evidence record
   543	
   544	A hardened operation emits exactly one record:
   545	
   546	```json
   547	{
   548	  "record_version": "hardened-capability-evidence-v1",
   549	  "hardened_profile": "hardened-profile-v1",
   550	  "execution_policy": "hardened-worker-v1",
   551	  "platform": "linux",
   552	  "enforcement_backend": "linux-namespace-seccomp-v1",
   553	  "qualification_status": "unqualified",
   554	  "outcome": "rejected",
   555	  "rejected_before": "domain-entry",
   556	  "diagnostic": "hardened_profile_unsupported",
   557	  "capabilities": [
   558	    {"name": "domain-membership-enforcement", "availability": "unprobed", "status": "not-applied", "probed_at": "pre-domain-entry"}
   559	  ],
   560	  "guarantees": [
   561	    {"name": "total-network-denial", "established": false}
   562	  ]
   563	}
   564	```
   565	
   566	The record contains exactly `record_version`, `hardened_profile`,
   567	`execution_policy`, `platform`, `enforcement_backend`, `qualification_status`,
   568	`outcome`, `rejected_before`, `diagnostic`, `capabilities`, and `guarantees`.
   569	`rejected_before` and `diagnostic` are `null` when `outcome` is `established`.
   570	
   571	`capabilities` contains exactly one entry per capability class of section 6.1,
   572	and each entry contains exactly `name`, `availability`, `status`, and
   573	`probed_at`. `availability` is `available`, `unavailable`, or `unprobed`.
   574	`status` is `applied` or `not-applied`. `probed_at` is `pre-domain-entry`.
   575	
   576	`guarantees` contains exactly one entry per guarantee of section 5, and each
   577	entry contains exactly `name` and `established`.
   578	
   579	Each condition below is an error, not a permitted variation:
   580	
   581	| Condition | Diagnostic |
   582	|---|---|
   583	| an `available` capability reported with a status other than `applied` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   584	| an `unavailable` or `unprobed` capability reported as `applied` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   585	| a missing, duplicated, extra, or unknown capability or guarantee entry | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   586	| an unknown `record_version` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   587	| `outcome: "established"` while any capability is not `applied` or any guarantee is not `established` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   588	| `outcome: "rejected"` without both `rejected_before` and `diagnostic` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   589	| a guarantee reported `established` while any class mapped to it by section 6.2 is not `applied` | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   590	| an availability value that was not obtained by a probe in this operation | `hardened_evidence_invalid` |
   591	| a portable `capability-evidence-v1` record emitted for a hardened operation, or this record emitted for a portable operation | `hardened_profile_claim_forbidden` |
   592	| an `execution_policy` other than `hardened-worker-v1`, or a `hardened_profile` other than `hardened-profile-v1` | `hardened_profile_claim_forbidden` |
   593	
   594	The record is result-only. It is exposed in install, dry-run plan, and status
   595	results, and it MUST NOT appear in a cache key, a receipt input, an install
   596	marker, or a conformance claim.
   597	
   598	## 7. Ordering and the fail-closed boundary
   599	
   600	### 7.1 Profile selection
   601	
   602	The hardened profile is selected by operator configuration or by a manager
   603	deployment mode. It MUST NOT be selected, requested, hinted, weakened, or
   604	disabled by a manifest value, a descriptor value, a build root, a source file,
   605	an environment value read from package data, or any other package-controlled
   606	byte.
   607	
   608	When the hardened profile is selected, a manager MUST NOT silently fall back to
   609	`manager-worker-v1`. If the hardened profile cannot be established, the
   610	operation rejects. An operator who wants the portable contract selects the
   611	portable profile explicitly, and that operation is a portable operation in every
   612	respect, including its cache key.
   613	
   614	### 7.2 Ordered phases
   615	
   616	A hardened operation MUST perform these phases in exactly this order. Package
   617	bytes reach a Go process only in phase 8 and later, and every phase from 8
   618	onward runs inside the build domain.
   619	
   620	| # | Phase | Rejection diagnostic |
   621	|---|---|---|
   622	| 1 | `profile-selection` | `hardened_profile_claim_forbidden` |
   623	| 2 | `platform-qualification` | `hardened_profile_unsupported` |
   624	| 3 | `capability-probe` | `hardened_capability_unavailable` |
   625	| 4 | `tcb-identity-verification` | `hardened_tcb_identity_invalid` |
   626	| 5 | `domain-establishment` | `hardened_domain_establishment_failed` |
   627	| 6 | `domain-guarantee-self-test` | `hardened_domain_establishment_failed` |
   628	| 7 | `domain-entry` | `hardened_domain_establishment_failed` |
   629	| 8 | `go-list` | `hardened_domain_breach_detected` |
   630	| 9 | `parent-graph-validation` | inherits `profiles/manager.md` section 2.3 |
   631	| 10 | `build-permit` | `hardened_domain_protocol_invalid` |
   632	| 11 | `go-build` | `hardened_domain_breach_detected` |
   633	| 12 | `artifact-verification` | inherits `protocol/core.md` section 9 |
   634	| 13 | `identity-reverification` | `hardened_tcb_identity_invalid` |
   635	| 14 | `domain-teardown` | `hardened_domain_breach_detected` |
   636	| 15 | `publication` | inherits `profiles/manager.md` section 2.5 |
   637	
   638	Phase 6 is a self-test performed from inside the freshly created domain, before
   639	any package byte is read by any process in it: the implementation MUST attempt,
   640	and MUST observe the kernel deny, at least one representative operation for each
   641	guarantee of section 5 that the platform declaration claims. A self-test that
   642	cannot be performed is a failure, not a pass.
   643	
   644	### 7.3 The failure boundary
   645	
   646	The hardened failure boundary is exact and strictly stronger than the portable
   647	one:
   648	
   649	- If the requested profile mixes hardened and portable identities, or asks for a
   650	  silent fallback, the operation rejects in phase 1 with
   651	  `hardened_profile_claim_forbidden`. If package data attempted to reach the
   652	  selection, it rejects with `hardened_package_influence_forbidden` instead.
   653	- If the platform is not qualified for the hardened profile, the operation
   654	  rejects in phase 2 with `hardened_profile_unsupported`.
   655	- If any capability class is unavailable, inconclusive, or unprobed, the
   656	  operation rejects in phase 3 with `hardened_capability_unavailable`.
   657	- If the TCB identities do not verify, the operation rejects in phase 4 with
   658	  `hardened_tcb_identity_invalid`.
   659	- If the domain cannot be created, a control cannot be applied, or a self-test
   660	  does not observe the expected denial, the operation rejects in phase 5 or 6
   661	  with `hardened_domain_establishment_failed`.
   662	
   663	Every one of those rejections happens **before domain entry** and therefore
   664	before `go list`, before `go build`, before any compiler, and before any package
   665	byte is read by any Go process. Every one of them publishes nothing, mutates no
   666	installation, consumer, marker, shim, or cache state, and leaves the
   667	installation byte-for-byte as it was.
   668	
   669	There is no partial hardened mode. A guarantee that cannot be established is
   670	never reported as best-effort, never downgraded to a warning, and never
   671	compensated for by a portable mechanism.
   672	
   673	### 7.4 Breach handling
   674	
   675	If, after domain entry, the implementation observes a guarantee violation — a
   676	domain escape, a write outside the private build root, an exec outside the
   677	allowlist, a network operation that succeeded, an exceeded aggregate bound, or a
   678	surviving domain member — it MUST tear the domain down, reject with
   679	`hardened_domain_breach_detected`, publish nothing, and MUST NOT reuse, adopt,
   680	cache, or record any byte produced by that operation.
   681	
   682	## 8. Cache, receipt, marker, and claim separation
   683	
   684	### 8.1 Cache identity
   685	
   686	The logical cache key is computed exactly as in `protocol/core.md` sections 9.1
   687	and 9.2, over the canonical build input whose policy object carries
   688	`execution_policy: "hardened-worker-v1"`.
   689	
   690	Consequently, for one identical source, command, target, and toolchain, three
   691	inputs produce three different keys and none of them aliases another:
   692	
   693	| Input | Execution policy | Key |
   694	|---|---|---|
   695	| pre-revision rc.4 candidate | absent | `sha256:3fcd714a40e8918eb67dbd35d435875dcce6c9047da811a1fa26626e5e57be48` |
   696	| portable | `manager-worker-v1` | `sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b` |
   697	| hardened | `hardened-worker-v1` | `sha256:13736230d33ce59de7f7323dcd4cffd510655ad8dabd5ee9e8b6cb182ec70037` |
   698	
   699	A reader MUST treat an entry whose execution policy is not the policy it
   700	implements for this operation as a miss. A hardened operation MUST NOT accept a
   701	portable entry, a portable operation MUST NOT accept a hardened entry, and
   702	neither MUST upgrade, downgrade, re-label, or re-sign an existing entry in
   703	place. A manager that implements both profiles MUST keep their entries logically
   704	disjoint and MUST revalidate the protected-cache boundary of `protocol/core.md`
   705	section 9.3 for each profile independently.
   706	
   707	Neither the hardened capability-evidence record, nor the TCB record, nor the
   708	enforcement backend, nor the platform participates in the cache key or in the
   709	hit comparison.
   710	
   711	### 8.2 Receipts
   712	
   713	A hardened local `go-v1` build writes **build receipt schema 3**. A hardened
   714	external `go-repository-v1` build writes **build receipt schema 4**. Both keep
   715	the exact receipt structure of `protocol/core.md` sections 9.1 and 9.2 — schema
   716	version, logical cache key, complete build input, and artifact path, SHA-256, and
   717	byte length — and both carry the hardened execution-policy identity inside the
   718	input.
   719	
   720	Receipt schemas 1 and 2 remain exactly as candidate `1.0.0-rc.5` defines them
   721	and MUST NOT be widened. A reader that does not implement the hardened profile
   722	MUST reject receipt schema 3 and 4 as unsupported receipt identities under
   723	`protocol/core.md` section 9.3; it MUST NOT parse them leniently, convert them,
